Privacy Policy
App: Periodic Table Pro
Effective date: June 07 2026
Contact: [CONTACT EMAIL]

This Privacy Policy explains how Periodic Table Pro (the "App") handles information. We have designed the App to work offline and to collect as little data as possible. By using the App, you agree to this policy.

Summary

We do not require an account and do not ask for your name, email, or any personal details.
Your favourites, notes, and settings are stored only on your device. We do not upload them.
The App can show element photos from Wikimedia and open Wikipedia in your browser, which involves standard internet requests to those services.
The App may display ads through Google AdMob, which may use a device advertising identifier.
Information We Collect

Information you provide. The App lets you save favourite elements and write personal notes. This content is stored locally on your device and is not transmitted to us or any third party. It is removed when you clear the App's data or uninstall the App.

Information collected automatically. The App itself contains no proprietary analytics or tracking. However:

Internet requests: When you view an element photo, the App requests that image from Wikimedia Commons; when you tap a "Wikipedia"/"Learn more" link, your device opens that page in your browser. As with any internet request, the destination servers may receive your device's IP address, the requested URL, and basic technical information in their normal logs.
Advertising (if enabled): The App may use Google AdMob to display ads. Advertising providers may collect or receive information such as a device advertising identifier and ad-interaction and device data to serve and measure ads.
We do not knowingly collect precise location, contacts, photos, microphone, or camera data.

How We Use Information

To provide core features (display elements, save favourites and notes, remember settings).
To load optional element images and open reference links you tap.
To display and measure advertising, if ads are enabled.
Advertising
If advertising is enabled, the App uses Google AdMob. Google may use a device advertising identifier and related data to serve personalized or non-personalized ads and to measure ad performance, per Google's policies (https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads). You can reset/delete your advertising ID and opt out of ad personalization in Settings → Privacy → Ads on Android. Where required by law, the App will request your consent before serving personalized ads.

Third-Party Services

Google Play Services / Google AdMob — https://policies.google.com/privacy
Wikimedia Commons / Wikipedia — https://foundation.wikimedia.org/wiki/Policy:Privacy_policy
We do not sell your personal information.

Data Retention and Deletion
We do not store your data on our servers. Favourites, notes, and settings live only on your device and are deleted when you clear the App's storage or uninstall the App.

Children's Privacy
The App is an educational reference for a general audience. It is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your country), and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. Any ads shown in child-directed contexts are intended to be non-personalized in accordance with applicable laws and Google Play's Families policy.

Security
Because the App keeps your content on your own device and does not transmit it to us, your data stays under your control. No method of storage is 100% secure, but we rely on Android's app sandboxing to protect locally stored data.

Your Rights
Depending on where you live (e.g., EU/UK GDPR or California CCPA/CPRA), you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal data. Because we do not hold personal data about you on our servers, most such data is fully under your control on your device. For advertising data handled by Google, use Google's privacy controls linked above or contact us.

Changes to This Policy
We may update this policy from time to time. Changes will be posted at this URL with a new effective date.
